.%20It's%20come%20at%20a%20cost%20to%20her%20savings%20and%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhow-to-take-mental-health-leave-fmla-ada-employment-lawyer-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3Eemotional%20well-being%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E.%20This%20interview%20has%20been%20edited%20for%20length%20and%20clarity.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20the%20youngest%20of%20five%20siblings.%20My%20mom%20held%20numerous%20jobs%20when%20we%20were%20little%2C%20and%20my%20dad%20worked%20in%20the%20city.%20When%20he%20worked%20strange%20hours%2C%20my%20older%20brother%20was%20the%20man%20of%20the%20house.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20mom%2C%20who%20worked%20for%20a%20surgeon%2C%20got%20me%20a%20job%20with%20his%20practice%2C%20where%20I%20worked%20for%2017%20years.%20My%20sister%20and%20I%20worked%20for%20my%20family's%20medical%20billing%20business.%20I%20also%20did%20insurance%20verification%2C%20and%20I'm%20currently%20in%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fcouldnt-find-job-at-45-going-to-nursing-school-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Enursing%20school%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20wish%20I%20had%20listened%20to%20my%20mom%20to%20pursue%20this%20when%20I%20was%2018.%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3Caside%3E%5Cn%3Cp%3EAre%20you%20paying%20for%20your%20own%20or%20your%20loved%20one's%20long-term%20care%3F%20Do%20you%20have%20thoughts%20to%20share%20about%20long-term%20care%20in%20the%20US%3F%20To%20share%20your%20story%20with%20a%20reporter%2C%20%3Cstrong%3Eplease%20fill%20out%20this%20%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3Ca%20rel%3D%5C%22noopener%20noreferrer%20nofollow%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.google.com%2Fforms%2Fd%2Fe%2F1FAIpQLSdg4AoiQ9q9GU2sU75z7cCrHvjt0JnM_0Nf34JYn_1DpF3w6A%2Fviewform%3Fusp%3Ddialog%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3Equick%20form%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cstrong%3E.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3C%2Faside%3E%5Cn%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%223d8fec92-338c-47c8-a593-f43d0df6a441%5C%22%3EI've%20been%20my%20family's%20caregiver%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20the%20last%20two%20decades%2C%20I've%20been%20on%20and%20off%20working%20because%20of%20my%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Faging-at-home-family-caregiving-costs-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Efamily's%20illnesses%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20was%20the%20one%20who%20wouldn't%20work%20anymore%20and%20stay%20home%20to%20take%20care%20of%20my%20father.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%202002%2C%20my%20son%20was%20an%20infant%20when%20my%20dad%20was%20rushed%20to%20the%20hospital.%20We%20had%20a%20cardiologist%20come%20see%20him%2C%20and%20he%20pulled%20strings%20to%20get%20my%20father%20into%20a%20Manhattan%20hospital.%20He%20wound%20up%20having%20open-heart%20surgery%20after%20doctors%20discovered%20he%20had%20a%20widowmaker%20heart%20attack.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EDoctors%20told%20us%20he%20had%20six%20months%20to%20a%20year%20at%20the%20most%2C%20but%20he%20wound%20up%20sticking%20around%20for%20six%20more%20years.%20His%20body%20took%20a%20toll%20little%20by%20little%2C%20and%20he%20started%20having%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmicroplastics-artery-plaque-mysterious-link-stroke-heart-attack-2025-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emini%20strokes%3C%2Fa%3E.%20He%20was%20basically%20homebound%2C%20and%20my%20mom%20would%20stay%20home%20with%20him.%20If%20she%20weren't%20there%2C%20I%20would%20be.%20I%20lived%20with%20them%20at%20that%20point.%20He%20would%20fall%20constantly%2C%20and%20we%20would%20have%20to%20rush%20to%20him%20frequently%20over%20a%20period%20of%20two%20months%20before%20he%20died%20in%202008.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20husband%20died%20in%20July%20that%20same%20year.%20It%20was%20completely%20unexpected.%20The%20hospital%20considered%20his%20mom%20and%20dad%20as%20the%20next%20of%20kin%2C%20and%20they%20kept%20him%20alive%20for%20four%20days%20while%20checking%20his%20organs%20for%20donation.%20It%20was%20too%20much%20for%20me.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShortly%20after%20that%2C%20my%20father-in-law%20was%20diagnosed%20with%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fprostate-cancer-breakthroughs-in-2025-pills-hormone-treatments-2025-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eprostate%20cancer%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20took%20him%20to%20the%20hospital%20for%20radiation%20therapy%20and%20handled%20some%20of%20his%20errands%2C%20as%20he%20only%20had%20his%20sister%20in%20the%20US%2C%20who%20lived%20in%20Florida.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWhen%20my%20father-in-law%20became%20sick%20again%20in%202021%2C%20we%20got%20him%20into%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flong-term-care-costs-growing-problem-for-americans-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Enursing%20home%3C%2Fa%3E%20because%20he%20couldn't%20care%20for%20himself%20anymore.%20I've%20dealt%20with%20all%20the%20red%20tape%20for%20him%2C%20and%20I%20became%20his%20power%20of%20attorney.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20was%20able%20to%20get%20Family%20and%20Medical%20Leave%20Act%20money%2C%20and%20when%20that%20ran%20out%2C%20I%20went%20back%20to%20work.%20I%20couldn't%20handle%20it%20anymore%20because%20of%20how%20many%20calls%20the%20nursing%20home%20gave%20me.%20I%20had%20some%20money%20saved%20up%20and%20had%20a%20401(k)%20I%20wound%20up%20using.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22ee3f557f-363e-43dc-b182-f63b6ed404bf%5C%22%3EI%20used%20up%20my%20retirement%20money%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EThen%2C%20my%20aunt%20was%20diagnosed%20with%20pancreatic%20cancer%2C%20and%20I%20became%20her%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flong-term-care-housing-adu-caregiving-working-full-time-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Efull-time%20caregiver%3C%2Fa%3E%20at%20that%20point.%20I%20took%20her%20to%20her%20chemo%20appointments%2C%20and%20I%20would%20stay%20with%20her%20for%20four%20to%20six%20hours%20after%20each%20treatment%20to%20make%20sure%20that%20she%20wasn't%20getting%20sick.%20Being%20out%20of%20a%20job%20wasn't%20so%20bad%2C%20and%20they%20would%20give%20me%20some%20money%20for%20my%20caregiving.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAfter%20she%20completed%20her%20chemo%2C%20she%20fell%20and%20needed%20back%20surgery%20to%20fuse%20two%20of%20her%20vertebrae.%20I%20became%20her%20caregiver%20again%2C%20and%20I%20would%20do%20her%20wound%20care.%20She%20recovered%20quite%20a%20bit%2C%20and%20we%20decided%20that%20she%20would%20do%20OK%20with%20just%20a%20cane.%20For%20a%20few%20years%20afterward%2C%20I%20wasn't%20a%20full-time%20caregiver%2C%20and%20I%20moved%20to%20Tennessee%20with%20my%20kids%20for%20a%20year.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20sister%20arranged%20a%20trip%20for%20my%20mom%20to%20go%20to%20Georgia%20to%20see%20her%20niece%20and%20nephew.%20She%20broke%20her%20pelvis%20while%20there%2C%20as%20well%20as%20her%20thigh%20bone%2C%20a%20few%20bones%2C%20and%20her%20wrist.%20After%20three%20days%20of%20arguing%20about%20what%20to%20do%2C%20we%20got%20her%20into%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fluxury-crypto-addiction-rehab-centers-price-photos-2023-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Erehab%20facility%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Her%20mind%20was%20slipping%20quite%20a%20bit.%20My%20siblings%20and%20I%20made%20sure%20my%20mom%20had%20everything%20she%20needed.%20After%20trying%20out%20aides%20who%20were%20not%20helpful%2C%20my%20sisters%20and%20I%20moved%20in%20with%20my%20mom%20on%20a%20rotating%20schedule%2C%2024%2F7.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShe%20didn't%20know%20where%20she%20was%20or%20who%20the%20people%20were.%20This%20probably%20lasted%20for%20a%20year%20and%20a%20half.%20At%20the%20start%20of%20the%20pandemic%2C%20she%20broke%20her%20femur%2C%20and%20she%20was%20only%20in%20the%20hospital.%20We%20got%20a%20hoist%20lift%2C%20but%20she%20really%20degraded%20quite%20a%20bit.%20She%20died%20in%202021.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20aunt%20offered%20for%20my%20kids%20and%20me%20to%20live%20here%20permanently%2C%20but%20it%20became%20obvious%20very%20quickly%20that%20she%20was%20developing%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Felder-care-dementia-cancer-ai-vibe-coding-claude-lovable-cursor-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EAlzheimer's%20disease%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20would%20have%20to%20babysit%20her%20all%20day%20to%20make%20sure%20she%20wasn't%20getting%20scammed%20or%20doing%20anything%20wrong.%20I%20had%20to%20take%20over%20control%20of%20her%20medication.%20I%20hired%20an%20aide%20to%20take%20her%20out%20during%20the%20day%20to%20give%20me%20a%20break%2C%20and%20that%20went%20on%20for%20a%20year%20and%20a%20half.%20Then%2C%20we%20took%20the%20car%20away%20from%20her.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOne%20day%20at%20the%20mall%2C%20she%20fell%20and%20broke%20her%20femur.%20She%20went%20to%20rehab%2C%20and%20I%20got%20her%20placed%20at%20an%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fretirement-long-term-care-expenses-assisted-living-bought-house-independence-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eassisted%20living%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20which%20I%20haven't%20been%20thrilled%20about.%20She's%20been%20there%20for%20about%20a%20year.%20There%20hasn't%20been%20much%20for%20me%20to%20do%20in%20her%20case%2C%20and%20I%20know%20I%20should%20be%20more%20active%2C%20but%20I%20can't%20handle%20it.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20became%20her%20trustee%2C%20and%20I%20get%20a%20living%20stipend%20that%20I%20draw%20on%2C%20which%20is%20enough%20to%20get%20by.%20I%20don't%20have%20to%20pay%20for%20her%20house.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20caring%20for%20my%20mother-in-law%2C%20who%20is%2085%2C%20and%20is%20not%20requiring%20any%20medical%20care%20except%20for%20driving%20her%20to%20all%20of%20her%20doctors.%20I've%20taken%20over%20her%20bills%20and%20mail%20because%20she%20can't%20see%20very%20well.%20I'm%20there%20to%20clean%20the%20house%20and%20fix%20anything.%20I'm%20probably%20with%20her%20for%20four%20hours%2C%20three%20times%20a%20week.%20I'd%20suspect%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Feldercare-crisis-long-term-care-costs-families-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ecaregiving%20costs%3C%2Fa%3E%20are%20between%20%241%2C000%20and%20%242%2C000%20monthly.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22f8bdf0d4-f187-463a-8b7d-7bfebd95352f%5C%22%3EI'm%20waiting%20for%20my%20life%20to%20start%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20taking%20it%20one%20day%20at%20a%20time.%20I%20don't%20have%20any%20plans%20for%20my%20life%20except%20taking%20care%20of%20my%20mother-in-law.%20When%20she's%20no%20longer%20here%2C%20that's%20when%20my%20life%20will%20start.%20I'm%20hoping%20to%20complete%20nursing%20school%20and%20find%20a%20good%20job%20somewhere%2C%20ideally%20traveling%20to%20people's%20homes%20to%20care%20for%20their%20physical%20needs.%20This%20way%2C%20I'll%20have%20something%20to%20support%20myself.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20still%20haven't%20dealt%20with%20the%20loss%20of%20my%20parents%2C%20my%20husband%2C%20or%20my%20father-in-law.%20It's%20just%20been%20putting%20up%20a%20wall%20and%20going%20on%20to%20the%20next%20person%20who%20needs%20help.%20It's%20very%20taxing%20and%20emotionally%20draining.%20You%20do%20what%20you%20have%20to%20do%20to%20get%20through%20the%20day%20and%20go%20on%20to%20the%20next%20one.%20I%20have%20a%20new%20granddaughter%2C%20who%20has%20been%20the%20light%20of%20my%20life.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20tell%20people%20that%20when%20you're%2018%2C%20buy%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fearly-retirement-long-term-care-costs-raising-children-savings-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Elong-term%20care%20insurance%3C%2Fa%3E.%20By%20the%20time%20you%20need%20it%2C%20you%20won't%20be%20able%20to%20afford%20it.%20I'm%2054%20and%20can't%20pay%20%24800%20a%20month.%20I'm%20better%20off%20being%20a%20Medicaid%20recipient%20so%20I%20don't%20have%20to%20worry%20about%20nursing%20homes.%20It's%20important%20to%20stay%20close%20to%20your%20family%20because%20you're%20going%20to%20need%20them.%20It%20goes%20a%20long%20way%20for%20mental%20health.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%