after%20a%20long%20time%20away%20and%20was%20surprised%20by%20how%20much%20it%20has%20changed.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EI%20felt%20like%20an%20outsider%2C%20and%20realized%20I%20had%20changed%20even%20more.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EI%20grew%20up%20in%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fbest-things-i-did-in-mexico-city-mistakes-to-avoid-2026-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EMexico%20City%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20spent%20most%20of%20my%20life%20there.%20Six%20years%20ago%2C%20I%20left%20the%20country%2C%20first%20for%20the%20US%20and%20later%20for%20the%20UK%2C%20but%20I%20never%20stopped%20thinking%20of%20my%20birthplace%20as%20the%20place%20I%20ultimately%20belonged.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20summer%2C%20I%20returned%20after%20two%20years%20away%2C%20the%20longest%20stretch%20I%20had%20ever%20gone%20without%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fbought-cheap-house-in-italy-village-before-visiting-risky-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Evisiting%20home%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20expected%20the%20trip%20to%20feel%20nostalgic%20and%20effortless.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EInstead%2C%20I%20was%20surprised%20by%20how%20tiring%20it%20felt%20and%2C%20for%20the%20first%20time%2C%20how%20slightly%20out%20of%20place%20I%20seemed%20to%20be.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%229c7677c6-dcb4-4fb3-b2d0-6d48eef00960%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EMexico%20City%20had%20changed%20while%20I%20was%20away%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20first%20thing%20that%20struck%20me%20was%20how%20different%20the%20city%20itself%20felt.%20Mexico%20City%20had%20always%20been%20huge%2C%20chaotic%2C%20and%20international%20in%20its%20own%20way%2C%20but%20the%20version%20I%20returned%20to%20felt%20noticeably%20more%20cosmopolitan%20than%20the%20one%20I%20remembered.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThere%20were%20new%20restaurants%20everywhere%2C%20more%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Famericas-most-innovative-businesses-2027-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Einternational%20businesses%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20more%20English%20being%20spoken%20around%20me%2C%20and%20far%20more%20foreigners%20than%20I%20remembered%20seeing%20before%20I%20left.%20Areas%20that%20once%20felt%20deeply%20familiar%20now%20seemed%20to%20belong%20to%20a%20newer%20version%20of%20the%20city.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20did%20not%20necessarily%20dislike%20any%20of%20it.%20But%20it%20surprised%20me%20how%20quickly%20I%20started%20feeling%20like%20someone%20who%20had%20missed%20a%20chapter.%20I%20was%20the%20one%20asking%20what%20had%20opened%2C%20what%20had%20closed%2C%20where%20people%20went%20now%2C%20and%20which%20places%20had%20become%20popular.%20For%20the%20first%20time%2C%20I%20was%20not%20the%20person%20who%20knew%20instinctively%20how%20the%20city%20worked.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20was%20strange%20because%20I%20had%20always%20thought%20of%20Mexico%20City%20as%20something%20fixed%20in%20my%20life.%20I%20was%20the%20one%20who%20had%20moved%20away%2C%20so%20part%20of%20me%20had%20unconsciously%20expected%20it%20to%20remain%20roughly%20as%20I%20had%20left%20it.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22cd632b49-c28f-4504-905b-c53ba7374139%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EThe%20city%20had%20changed%2C%20but%20many%20of%20the%20people%20I%20knew%20somehow%20hadn't%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMexico%20City%20felt%20almost%20unrecognizable%20in%20places%2C%20but%20spending%20time%20with%20people%20I%20had%20known%20for%20years%20created%20the%20opposite%20sensation.%20Despite%20all%20the%20time%20that%20had%20passed%2C%20some%20conversations%20felt%20as%20though%20I%20had%20only%20been%20away%20for%20a%20few%20weeks.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOn%20paper%2C%20a%20lot%20had%20changed.%20Friends%20had%20gotten%20married%2C%20moved%20in%20with%20partners%2C%20started%20having%20children%2C%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fjob-growth-losses-august-industries-labor-market-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Echanged%20jobs%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20taken%20on%20responsibilities%20that%20did%20not%20exist%20when%20we%20were%20younger.%20Their%20lives%20had%20clearly%20moved%20forward.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAnd%20yet%2C%20with%20certain%20exceptions%2C%20I%20sometimes%20found%20myself%20listening%20to%20the%20same%20stories%2C%20the%20same%20frustrations%2C%20and%20even%20the%20same%20problems%20I%20remembered%20from%20years%20earlier.%20Certain%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsigns-youre-in-a-strong-relationship-2017-2%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Erelationship%20dynamics%3C%2Fa%3E%20had%20barely%20shifted.%20People%20worried%20about%20versions%20of%20the%20same%20things%20they%20had%20worried%20about%20before%20I%20left.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIt%20was%20a%20strange%20feeling.%20I%20had%20expected%20two%20years%20away%20to%20make%20everyone%20seem%20dramatically%20different%2C%20particularly%20because%20so%20many%20of%20them%20had%20crossed%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsupported-my-partner-business-dreams-what-it-cost-me-relationship-2026-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Emajor%20life%20milestones%3C%2Fa%3E%20in%20that%20time.%20Instead%2C%20I%20often%20recognized%20not%20just%20the%20people%20themselves%2C%20but%20the%20exact%20patterns%20I%20remembered.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThere%20was%20something%20comforting%20about%20that%20familiarity%2C%20but%20also%20something%20disorienting.%20The%20city%20around%20us%20seemed%20to%20have%20accelerated%2C%20while%20parts%20of%20the%20social%20world%20I%20had%20left%20behind%20felt%20almost%20preserved.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20contrast%20eventually%20forced%20me%20to%20consider%20another%20possibility.%20Maybe%20the%20reason%20everything%20felt%20so%20different%20to%20me%20was%20not%20because%20everyone%20else%20had%20changed%20beyond%20recognition.%20Maybe%20I%20had.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22b126dc0b-777c-4fc8-b7e7-9f59f032b078%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EI%20realized%20the%20biggest%20change%20was%20me%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20last%20two%20years%20have%20probably%20changed%20me%20more%20than%20I%20understood%20before%20this%20trip.%20My%20relationship%20became%20more%20serious%2C%20and%20my%20partner%20and%20I%20started%20living%20together%2C%20which%20altered%20the%20rhythm%20of%20my%20everyday%20life%20in%20ways%20that%20felt%20gradual%20at%20the%20time%20but%20obvious%20once%20I%20stepped%20away%20from%20them.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20no%20longer%20organize%20my%20days%20entirely%20around%20myself.%20We%20make%20plans%20together%2C%20decide%20how%20to%20spend%20our%20weekends%2C%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ffirst-long-couple-trip-togther-early-in-relationship-worked-tips-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Etravel%20as%20a%20couple%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20share%20responsibilities%2C%20and%20build%20routines%20around%20one%20another.%20Even%20the%20boring%20parts%20of%20life%2C%20like%20deciding%20what%20to%20eat%20or%20how%20to%20spend%20a%20quiet%20evening%2C%20have%20become%20part%20of%20a%20shared%20structure.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBeing%20back%20in%20Mexico%20made%20me%20notice%20how%20attached%20I%20had%20become%20to%20that%20structure.%20I%20missed%20my%20apartment%2C%20my%20work%20routine%2C%20my%20evenings%20with%20my%20partner%2C%20and%20even%20the%20ordinary%20habits%20I%20would%20never%20normally%20think%20were%20worth%20missing.%20The%20things%20pulling%20me%20back%20were%20not%20landmarks%20or%20anything%20particularly%20British.%20They%20were%20simply%20the%20details%20of%20the%20life%20I%20had%20built.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20realization%20helped%20explain%20why%20the%20trip%20had%20felt%20so%20tiring%20and%20unfamiliar.%20Mexico%20was%20still%20deeply%20important%20to%20me%2C%20and%20the%20people%20I%20loved%20there%20were%20still%20part%20of%20who%20I%20was%2C%20but%20the%20center%20of%20my%20everyday%20existence%20had%20shifted%20somewhere%20else.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20years%2C%20I%20thought%20of%20myself%20as%20someone%20w